WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
Picture an insurance market where
wealthy people back the policies

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.750
with everything they own.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.360
At Lloyd's of London, these
backers were called Names.

4
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:16.700
Losses in 1989, 1990 and 1991
were each over 2 billion pounds.

5
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.880
Many Names faced heavy losses,

6
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.800
and some were ruined.

7
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.180
So if a business you own goes bust,

8
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.460
could you lose your home as well?

9
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.510
In this mission, you'll see how
banks turn savings into loans,

10
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.300
and why some borrowers
pay more than others.

11
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.940
Then you'll weigh up loans,

12
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:39.190
overdrafts, shares and crowdfunding,
and match each one to the right job.

13
00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:42.290
Your mission: find out who
really carries the risk

14
00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.650
when a business fails.
